   755→--[[ Types:header
   756→
   757→## SettingObject ![](https://img.shields.io/badge/object-teal)
   758→
   759→Table containing the following entries:
   760→
   761→| key      | value                                  | type                        | required |
   762→|:---------|:---------------------------------------|:----------------------------|:---------|
   763→| kind     | setting type                           | [SettingType](#settingtype) | yes      |
   764→| name     | label for the setting                  | string                      | yes      |
   765→| desc     | description for the setting            | string                      | no       |
   766→| default  | default value for the setting          | any                         | yes      |
   767→| get      | getter for the current value           | function                    | yes      |
   768→| set      | setter for the new value               | function                    | yes      |
   769→| disabled | whether the setting should be disabled | boolean                     | no       |
   770→
   771→- The getter passes `layoutName` as the sole argument and expects a value in return.
   772→- The setter passes (`layoutName`, `newValue`, `fromReset`) and expects no returns.
   773→- The description is shown in a tooltip.
   774→
   775→Depending on the setting type there are additional required and optional entries:
   776→
   777→### Dropdown ![](https://img.shields.io/badge/object-teal)
   778→
   779→| key       | value                                                                                                                 | type     | required |
   780→|:----------|:----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|:---------|:---------|
   781→| values    | indexed table containing [DropdownOption](#dropdownoption)s                                                           | table    | no       |
   782→| multiple  | whether the dropdown should allow selecing multiple options                                                           | boolean  | no       |
   783→| generator | [Dropdown `SetupMenu` "generator" (callback)](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Patch_11.0.0/API_changes#New_menu_system) | function | no       |
   784→| height    | max height of the menu                                                                                                | integer  | no       |
   785→
   786→- Either `values` or `generator` is required, the former for simple menues and the latter for complex ones.
   787→    - They are not exclusive, but `generator` takes precedence (e.g. `values` will be available but not used).
   788→- `generator` signature is `(dropdown, rootDescription, settingObject)` - `settingObject` being the addition to the default arguments.
   789→	- getters and setters are not handled using `generator`, and must be handled by the layout
   790→
   791→## DropdownOption ![](https://img.shields.io/badge/object-teal)
   792→
   793→Table containing the following entries:
   794→
   795→| key     | value                                                              | type    | required |
   796→|:--------|:-------------------------------------------------------------------|---------|:---------|
   797→| text    | text rendered in the dropdown                                      | string  | yes      |
   798→| value   | value the text represents, defaults to the text if not provided    | any     | no       |
   799→
   800→### Slider ![](https://img.shields.io/badge/object-teal)
   801→
   802→| key       | value                             | type     | required | default |
   803→|:----------|:----------------------------------|:---------|:---------|:--------|
   804→| minValue  | lower bound for the slider        | number   | no       | 0       |
   805→| maxValue  | upper bound for the slider        | number   | no       | 1       |
   806→| valueStep | step increment between each value | number   | no       | 1       |
   807→| formatter | formatter for the display value   | function | no       |         |
   808→
   809→- The formatter passes `value` as the sole argument and expects a number value in return.
   810→
   811→### ColorPicker ![](https://img.shields.io/badge/object-teal)
   812→
   813→| key        | value                            | type    | required | default |
   814→|:-----------|:---------------------------------|:--------|:---------|:--------|
   815→| hasOpacity | whether or not to enable opacity | boolean | no       | false   |
   816→
   817→The `default` field and the getter expects a [ColorMixin](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/ColorMixin) object, and the setter will pass one as its value.
   818→Even if `hasOpacity` is set to `false` (which is the default value) the ColorMixin object will contain an alpha value, this is the default behavior of the ColorMixin.
   819→
   820→## ButtonObject ![](https://img.shields.io/badge/object-teal)
   821→
   822→Table containing the following entries:
   823→
   824→| key   | value                           | type     | required |
   825→|:------|:--------------------------------|----------|:---------|
   826→| text  | text rendered on the button     | string   | yes      |
   827→| click | callback when button is clicked | function | yes      |
   828→
   829→## SettingType ![](https://img.shields.io/badge/object-teal)
   830→Table containing available setting types.
   831→
   832→One of:
   833→- `Dropdown`
   834→- `Checkbox`
   835→- `Slider`
   836→- `Divider`
   837→- `ColorPicker`
   838→--]]
   839→lib.SettingType = CopyTable(Enum.EditModeSettingDisplayType)
   840→lib.SettingType.ColorPicker = 10 -- leave some room for blizzard expansion
   841→
```

